{
  "case_id": "2020-19-422",
  "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0000-0009",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the Third Amendment, FHFA, acting as conservator of Fannie and Freddie, renegotiated the enterprises' financial obligations to Treasury by replacing the enterprises' multibillion-dollar dividend and fee obligations with a variable dividend tied to their net worth."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Federal parties",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, both claims are barred by the Recovery Act's succession clause, which transfers to the conservator the authority to decide whether shareholders may bring derivative suits on behalf of the enterprises. The type of shareholder injury alleged here, that the corporations' assets have been unlawfully dissipated to a particular shareholder, is plainly derivative rather than direct. The shareholders have not cited even a single case to the contrary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Federal parties",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Second, the statutory claim is barred by the Recovery Act's anti-injunction clause, which prevents courts from restraining exercises of the conservator's powers or functions. The conservator acted well within its authority in deciding that the renegotiation of the enterprises' financial obligations may have been appropriate to preserve and conserve Treasury's capital commitment. The shareholders cannot second-guess the wisdom or motives behind that business judgment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If we agree with you about the removability of an acting director and also agree with you that the only relevant action was one taken by the acting director, would we have any reason to address the question whether the restriction on the removal of a confirmed director is constitutional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Federal parties",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0000-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MOOPPAN: Your Honor, it's because the shareholders' harm is derivative of the harm to the corporation. All they have lost --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If that's the case, that that's the only final action challenged here, what basis would we have to do anything more than issue a -- a -- a declaratory judgment about the validity of that amendment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the plaintiffs in this case did seek a declaratory judgment that the structure of the FH -- FHFA was unconstitutional, and the Fifth Circuit granted them that relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So it's a merits -- a merits determination then?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Aaron L. Nielson",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is a very easy way to answer the constitutional question in this case. The Court should hold that unless Congress says so in a statute, an acting director does not have tenure full stop."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Well, there were contracts before the Third Amendment too and they were significantly altered, but I guess my question is what if the complaining stockholders here, you know, sent a letter to the director, the confirmed one, and said we want you to get out of this agreement because it's unfair to us, and the director said no?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Nielson",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, nothing like that is in the complaint. There's no complaint about this Heritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Nielson",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, beyond that, this isn't an ordinary agency action where you could, like, file a petition for rulemaking or something like that. It's a contract, and, sure, the parties could renegotiate the contract, but it takes two to tango, and it's not just the decision of the -- of the FHFA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And two is, let's -- let's box in that, let's assume that's the case. So what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Thompson",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Net Worth Sleep -- Sweep leaves Fannie and Freddie with no reasonable prospect of becoming adequately capitalized, and so long as it remains in place, the companies' best-case scenario is to operate with so little capital that under Section 4617(a)(3), FHFA could place them into receivership at any time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are two distinct injuries caused by the Net Worth Sweep, one suffered by the companies, which cannot rebuild capital and return to a sound condition, and another suffered by private shareholders who were moved -- were removed from the companies' capital structures."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Thompson",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Net Worth Sweep exposed that line of commitment to maximum vulnerability because the companies can never build up capital to absorb losses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. Mr. Thompson, the -- both the government and amicus point out that your complaint only notes or -- or focuses on the adoption of Amendment III, or the Third Amendment. I admit that, obviously, your -- your prayer for relief speaks in injunctive relief, as you just noted. But would you spend a few minutes on that, should -- as to how we read in continuing implementation of the amendment and future implementation of the amendment when you only complain of the adoption of the amendment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 80,
        "start": 80
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I want to follow up a little bit on Justice Alito's questions. It does seem counterintuitive, perhaps illogical, to say that assuming you're right that the FHFA director must be removable at will, why you should get anything more than a gen -- than a declaratory judgment to that effect."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "just go back to Justice Alito's question about the Social Security Administration. I'll put some scary sounding numbers on this."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Don't you think it's a little bit odd because, I mean, none of us really think that any of those decisions would be different if there were a different level of presidential supervision, do we?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0004-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I mean, in a case like this, Mr. Thompson, where we're trying to figure out the proper remedy, I mean, it's -- it's -- it's a -- it's a kind of equitable question, isn't it, and we're trying to figure out what position you would have been in absent a constitutional violation. Why -- why isn't that"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0004-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does that mean, Mr. Thompson, that we have to do a great deal more than invalidate the -- the -- the Third Amendment and everything that follows from it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0004-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I -- I guess I don't understand that latter answer, a -- a lot of facts in there. But what legally, what constitutionally would prohibit ratification?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0004-0007",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 95,
        "start": 95
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The amicus points out that Seila Law used the phrase \"significant executive power.\" Your response to that? Was that a descriptor, descriptive language, or -- or is that a necessary condition before we can say that a for-cause removal restriction on an executive officer is unconstitutional? The amicus says the latter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0005-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 104,
        "start": 104
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I point the Court to J.A. 179 and 180, which says: \"To the extent not paid, pursuant to Section 2A, dividends on shares shall accrue and shall be added to the liquidation preference whether or not the funds legally available for the payment of such dividends and whether or not dividends are declared.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Nielson",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0005-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 105,
        "start": 105
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Nielson, this Court appointed you to brief and argue the case as an amicus curiae in support of the position that the structure of the Federal Housing Finance Agency does not violate the separation of powers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-422",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b35da9b2c234f06ea445c98ef57c335f1dee514e1611ee1b2e7b108f1d829857",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b35da9b2c234-0005-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 105,
        "start": 105
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted.\n(Whereupon, at 11:41 a.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
    {
